<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asturia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Asturia was the Roman name for the lands of the Astures in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a>, covering modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a>, the province of León and neighbouring areas. Conquered in Augustus' <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantabrian-wars">Cantabrian Wars</a> of 29–19 BCE, it was soon attached to the province of Hispania Tarraconensis, with its centre at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturica-augusta">Asturica Augusta</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astorga">Astorga</a>). Its gold mines, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/las-medulas">Las Médulas</a>, made it a major source of imperial wealth.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/asturia.jpg" alt="Asturia" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Banderas · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Asturias.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
